WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.340
Your coding agent

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.100
just changed one button.

3
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.190
It read the code back,

4
00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.820
and said: done.

5
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:06.940
But on a phone,

6
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.700
that button just broke.

7
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.780
Agents write UI blind.

8
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.940
Arguseye gives them eyes.

9
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:13.740
Here's what happens

10
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.260
when your agent calls it.

11
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.260
Arguseye reads your project.

12
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.540
It finds the component,

13
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.820
every place it's used,

14
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.980
and the props your code passes it.

15
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.740
Then your layouts, theme,

16
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.540
global CSS, fonts, and images.

17
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.860
Your own packages are bundled once,

18
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.620
and Chromium draws the result.

19
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.900
No dev server.

20
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.500
Back come a screenshot,

21
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.860
the accessibility tree,

22
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.220
and what changed.

23
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.900
So the agent sees the break,

24
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.420
fixes it, and checks again.

25
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.860
Any component:

26
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.660
React, Next, or Vue.

27
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.980
And in VS Code,

28
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.340
it updates as you type.

29
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.100
It works with Claude Code,

30
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.380
Codex, Cursor,

31
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.820
and any MCP client.

32
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.140
Arguseye. Open source.

33
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.060
One command to install.
